/Alt (Diagram showing an exercise protocol for monitoring sweating responses. A sequence of icons depicts the timeline: at zero minutes, participants' nude body mass is measured. Between zero and fifteen minutes, 80% of maximum heart rate is achieved with initial patches set on the upper arm. Between thirty-five and fifty-five minutes, patch one is removed, and patch two is applied. By sixty to ninety-five minutes, patch two is removed. Temperature and humidity conditions differ: forty degrees Celsius with thirty percent and thirty degrees Celsius with eighty percent relative humidity. Legend shows S1, iButton, and patches one and two placement.)
/K [933 0 R 934 0 R 935 0 R 936 0 R 937 0 R 938 0 R 939 0 R]
/P 44 0 R
